#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:2
msgid "Desktop app troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:5
msgid "Broken shortcuts after upgrading to v6.1.0 (Windows MSI only)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:7
msgid ""
"After upgrading to Mattermost Desktop v6.1.0 using the Windows MSI "
"installer from an older release, the desktop or taskbar shortcut shows "
"the wrong icon or fails to launch. This is due to a one-time icon "
"handling change in the Windows MSI installer to improve shortcut "
"reliability for future upgrades."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:9
msgid ""
"This issue doesn't block app usage and only affects Windows MSI installer"
" upgrades from pre-v6.1.0 versions. Users can launch Mattermost from the "
"Start Menu or a working desktop shortcut.Future upgrades to v6.1.1 and "
"later will not require shortcut recreation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:11
msgid "To resolve this issue, recreate the shortcut:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:13
msgid ""
"Right-click the broken shortcut on the taskbar and select **Unpin from "
"taskbar**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:14
msgid ""
"Launch Mattermost Desktop from the Start Menu or a working desktop "
"shortcut."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:15
msgid ""
"Right-click the Mattermost icon in the taskbar while the application is "
"running."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:16
msgid "Select **Pin to taskbar**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:18
msgid "The new shortcut will work correctly for all future upgrades."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:20
msgid ""
"Organizations standardizing on Windows installations can choose between "
"Windows Store (recommended for automatic updates) or MSI packages "
"(traditional deployment). The MSI method includes this one-time shortcut "
"adjustment; the Windows Store method doesn't."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:23
msgid "Where is configuration stored locally?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:25
msgid ""
"The location of the Mattermost desktop app configuration file depends on "
"the platform where you're running Mattermost (and, in the case of macOS, "
"how you've chosen to install the app):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:27
msgid "Windows: ``Users\\<username>\\AppData\\Roaming\\Mattermost``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:28
msgid ""
"macOS installer: ``/Users/<username>/Library/Application "
"Support/Mattermost``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:29
msgid ""
"macOS App Store: "
"``/Users/<username>/Library/Containers/Mattermost.Desktop/Data/Library/Application"
" Support/Mattermost`` (via Finder: ``~/Library/Application "
"Support/Mattermost`` as the extension is hidden)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:30
msgid "Linux: ``~/.config/Mattermost``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:34
msgid ""
"Local configuration data is not automatically removed when uninstalling "
"the desktop app. If you wish to remove all data, you must manually remove"
" the files from the applicable location noted above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:35
msgid ""
"Prior to uninstalling, you can choose to log out of any active sessions. "
"You can terminate active sessions from another Mattermost session in "
"**Profile > Security > View and Logout of Active Sessions**, then select "
"**Log Out**. Desktop app sessions are labeled as **Native Desktop App**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:38
msgid "Update notifications not appearing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:40
msgid ""
"If you're not seeing in-app update notifications when new versions are "
"available:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:42
msgid ""
"**Check your internet connection**: Ensure outbound HTTPS communication "
"to ``mattermost.com`` is allowed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:44
msgid ""
"**Manually check for updates**: Go to **Help > Check for Updates** or "
"**Settings > General > Check for Updates Now** to trigger an immediate "
"check."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:46
msgid "**Verify update notifications are enabled**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:48
msgid ""
"On Windows: Go to **… > File > Settings** and ensure **Automatically "
"check for updates** is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:49
msgid ""
"On macOS: Go to **Mattermost > Settings** and ensure **Automatically "
"check for updates** is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:51
msgid ""
"**Check Group Policy settings** (Enterprise deployments): Your system "
"administrator may have disabled update notifications via the "
"``EnableAutoUpdates`` Group Policy. Contact your IT department for "
"clarification."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:53
msgid ""
"**Version previously skipped**: If you selected **Skip This Version** for"
" the current release, manually check for updates to see it again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:56
msgid "Update required screen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:58
msgid ""
"From Mattermost server v11.6.0, system admins can set a minimum Desktop "
"App version in **System Console > Site Configuration > Customization > "
"Minimum desktop app version**. If your Desktop App version is below the "
"configured minimum, you will see an update required screen and cannot "
"access Mattermost until you update."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:60
msgid ""
"The screen includes a **Download** button that links to the apps download"
" page configured by your admin. Select **Download** to go to that page, "
"then follow the :ref:`manual update steps <deployment-guide/desktop"
"/desktop-troubleshooting:how to manually update mattermost desktop>` for "
"your platform."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:62
msgid ""
"If you believe your app is already up to date, contact your system admin "
"to confirm the configured minimum version."
msgstr ""

