#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:105
msgid "How do I access logs?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:107
msgid ""
"From Mattermost desktop v5.3, you can access logs via **Help > Show "
"logs**, which opens the file manager window showing the location of the "
"log file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:110
msgid "How do I download app diagnostics?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:112
msgid ""
"From Mattermost desktop v5.3, you can download a diagnostics text file "
"via **Help > Run diagnostics**, which can be attached to a Support "
"ticket."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:115
msgid "Deep links open in the wrong workspace in multi-view"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:117
msgid ""
"If you experience deep links opening in the wrong workspace, ensure all "
"relevant workspaces are pre-provisioned via the Group Policy "
"``DefaultServerList``. See the :ref:`multi-view and group policies "
"<deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-msi-installer-and-group-policy-install"
":multi-view and Group Policies>` documentation for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:119
msgid ""
"Verify that workspace URLs match exactly (including protocol and "
"subdomain) so links route to the intended workspace."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:120
msgid ""
"Edit the workspace list to correct or remove stale entries, then retry "
"the link."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:123
msgid "High CPU or memory when multiple workspaces open"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:125
msgid ""
"Verify the device is powerful enough to run several workspaces "
"concurrently. Close unused tabs and pop-out windows to reduce load."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:127
msgid ""
"Check the :doc:`desktop app advanced settings </end-user-"
"guide/preferences/customize-desktop-app-experience>`. Toggle **Use GPU "
"hardware acceleration** off on systems with unstable drivers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:130
msgid ""
"Desktop App displays white screen while launching and doesn't load the "
"page"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:132
msgid ""
"Delete the local ``Mattermost desktop app`` configuration file. See the "
"`Where is configuration stored locally? <#where-is-configuration-stored-"
"locally>`__ section above for file location details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:133
msgid "Reinstall the application."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:138
msgid "Upgrade to v6.1.0 fails or installs duplicate version (Windows MSI)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:140
msgid ""
"After installing v6.1.0 MSI, the old version still appears, both versions"
" are present, or the upgrade doesn't seem to work. This is because you "
"had a per-user installation from v5.9 to v6.0.4. From v6.1.0, the MSI "
"installer defaults to per-machine (system-wide) installation. MSI "
"installers cannot automatically upgrade across different installation "
"contexts (per-user to per-machine)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:142
msgid "To check your installation type before upgrading, open File Explorer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:144
msgid ""
"If Mattermost is in ``C:\\Program Files\\Mattermost`` or ``C:\\Program "
"Files (x86)\\Mattermost``: Per-machine install (upgrade will work "
"normally)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:145
msgid ""
"If Mattermost is in ``C:\\Users\\<YourName>\\AppData\\Local\\...``: Per-"
"user install (requires manual uninstall before v6.1.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:147
msgid ""
"To resolve this issue, you must manually uninstall the old version before"
" installing v6.1.0:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:149
msgid "Uninstall both versions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:151
msgid "Go to **Settings > Apps** or **Control Panel > Programs and Features**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:152
msgid "Uninstall all Mattermost Desktop entries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:154
msgid ""
"Download the v6.1.0 MSI installer again from the `releases page "
"<https://github.com/mattermost/desktop/releases>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:155
msgid ""
"Install v6.1.0 with administrator privileges (it will install to "
"``C:\\Program Files\\Mattermost``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:156
msgid "Future upgrades will work normally."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:159
msgid "\"Installation has failed\" dialog"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:161
msgid ""
"The app data might be corrupted. Remove all the files in "
"``%LOCALAPPDATA%\\mattermost``, then try reinstalling the app."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:164
msgid "\"The application \"Mattermost\" can't be opened\" dialog"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:166
msgid ""
"On macOS Catalina, this dialog can be triggered if the Mac Archive "
"Utility is the default method for decompressing files. In this case using"
" a third-party tool such as `Keka <https://www.keka.io>`_ or `Unarchiver "
"<https://macpaw.com/the-unarchiver>`_ may resolve the problem."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:169
msgid "Desktop App window is black and doesn't load the page"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:171
#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:184
msgid "Ensure you have installed the latest desktop app version available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:172
msgid ""
"Clear your cache and reload the app from **View > Clear Cache and "
"Reload** or press :kbd:`Ctrl` :kbd:`Shift` :kbd:`R` on Windows or Linux, "
"or :kbd:`⌘` :kbd:`⇧` :kbd:`R` on Mac."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:173
msgid "Quit the app and restart it to see if the issue clears."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:174
msgid "Disable GPU hardware acceleration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:176
msgid ""
"On Windows or Linux, select **File > Settings** and clear the **Use GPU "
"hardware acceleration** option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:177
msgid ""
"On macOS, select **Mattermost > Settings** and clear the **Use GPU "
"hardware acceleration** option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:179
msgid ""
"If you are using a special video driver, such as Optimus, try disabling "
"it to see if the problem is resolved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:182
msgid "Desktop App window is white and doesn't load the page"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:185
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Delete the ``%userprofile%\\AppData\\Roaming\\Mattermost`` directory on "
"your local machine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:186
msgid "Reinstall the desktop app."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:189
msgid "Desktop App is not visible, but the Mattermost icon is in the Task Bar"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:191
msgid ""
"This issue can occur on Windows in a multiple-monitor setup. When you "
"disconnect the monitor that Mattermost is displayed on, Mattermost "
"continues to display at screen coordinates that no longer exist."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:193
msgid ""
"To resolve this issue, you can reset the desktop app screen location by "
"deleting the screen location file. When the file is not present, the "
"desktop app displays on the primary monitor by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:195
msgid "To reset the desktop app screen location:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:197
msgid ""
"If the desktop app is running, right-click the Mattermost icon in the "
"task bar, then select **Close Window**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:198
msgid ""
"Open Windows File Explorer, and go to the ``%APPDATA%\\Mattermost`` "
"folder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:199
msgid "Delete the file ``bounds-info.json``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:202
msgid "Desktop App constantly refreshes the page"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:204
msgid ""
"This issue can occur when ``localStorage`` has an unexpected state. To "
"resolve the issue:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:206
msgid ""
"Windows: Open Windows File Explorer, go to the ``%APPDATA%\\Mattermost`` "
"folder, then delete the ``Local Storage`` folder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:207
msgid ""
"Mac: Open Finder, go to the ``~/Library/Application Support/Mattermost`` "
"folder, then delete the ``Local Storage`` folder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:208
msgid ""
"Linux: Open the File Manager, go to the ``~/.config/Mattermost`` folder, "
"then delete the ``Local Storage`` folder. Linux file managers may hide "
"folders starting with a period by default. You can delete them from the "
"terminal using ``rm -rf ~/.config/Mattermost``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:211
msgid "Desktop App constantly asks to log in to Mattermost server"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:213
msgid ""
"This issue can occur after a crash or unexpected shutdown of the desktop "
"app that causes the app data to be corrupted. To resolve the issue:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:215
msgid ""
"Windows: Open Windows File Explorer, go to the ``%APPDATA%\\Mattermost`` "
"folder, then delete the ``IndexedDB`` folder and the ``Cookies`` and "
"``Cookies-journal`` files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:216
msgid ""
"Mac: Open Finder, go to the ``~/Library/Application Support/Mattermost`` "
"folder, then delete the ``IndexedDB`` folder and the ``Cookies`` and "
"``Cookies-journal`` files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:217
msgid ""
"Linux: Open the file manager, go to the ``~/.config/Mattermost`` folder, "
"then delete the ``IndexedDB`` folder and the ``Cookies`` and ``Cookies-"
"journal`` files. Linux file managers may hide folders starting with a "
"period by default. You can delete them from the terminal using ``rm -rf "
"~/.config/Mattermost``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:220
msgid "\"Internal error: BrowserWindow 'unresponsive' event has been emitted\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:222
msgid ""
"Selecting **Show Details** on the dialog provides logs. Ways to resolve "
"the issue:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:224
msgid ""
"Clear the cache via **View > Clear Cache and Reload** or press "
":kbd:`Ctrl` :kbd:`Shift` :kbd:`R` on Windows or Linux, or :kbd:`⌘` "
":kbd:`⇧` :kbd:`R` on Mac."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:225
msgid ""
"Go to App Settings via **File > Settings** (or by pressing :kbd:`Ctrl` "
":kbd:`,` on Windows or Linux, or :kbd:`⌘` :kbd:`,` on Mac) and unselect "
"hardware acceleration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:228
msgid ""
"Desktop app not responsive within Citrix Virtual Apps or Desktop "
"Environment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:230
msgid ""
"Append ``Mattermost.exe;`` to the Registry Key "
"``HKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\CtxUvi\\UviProcessExcludes``"
" and reboot the system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:232
msgid ""
"For further assistance, review the `Troubleshooting forum "
"<https://forum.mattermost.com/c/trouble-shoot/16>`_ for previously "
"reported errors, or `join the Mattermost user community for "
"troubleshooting help <https://mattermost.com/community/>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:235
msgid "Can I uninstall the desktop app I installed using snap on Linux?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:237
msgid ""
"Yes. Run the following command from a terminal window: ``sudo snap remove"
" mattermost-desktop``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:240
msgid "Report Desktop App issues"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/desktop/desktop-troubleshooting.rst:242
msgid ""
"When reporting issues found in the Mattermost desktop app, it's helpful "
"to include the contents of the Developer Tools Console along with `the "
